ntentLength":135137},"type":"attachment"},{"link":{"used":true,"missed":false,"id":"886efede54209e6b1ac67fefd66e9f09","originalFileName":"ab93b2e1-2bd8-4123-90b2-2fd3e4232118-attachment.png","ext":".png","contentType":"image/png","contentLength":159979,"name":"newspec-c/evidence/tc06-s21-s22-pixel7-nh-chart-encounter.png"},"type":"attachment"},{"link":{"used":true,"missed":false,"id":"f2b606606bf214071a184914bd496467","originalFileName":"17c20d44-2d2c-44d6-8690-f5a68875fc18-attachment.png","ext":".png","contentType":"image/png","contentLength":186353,"name":"newspec-c/evidence/tc06-s21-s22-pixel7-nh-chart-preround.png"},"type":"attachment"},{"link":{"used":true,"missed":false,"id":"41cbbe81e31f344ba100a28cff343501","originalFileName":"4720a68d-b0c4-4c74-8f2b-a5474bf4d447-attachment.json","ext":".json","contentType":"application/json","contentLength":5205,"name":"lane result (newspec-c/results.json)"},"type":"attachment"}],"error":{"message":"newspec-c: record-only → passed (record only (every judged cell passed, the rest is recorded only))\nOur own addition (no UAT item or ticket asks for axe): record-only, findings are suggestions. Spec newspec-c/vis-tc06-s21-s22-badge-visual.spec.ts ran axe-core 4.14 (WCAG 2 A/AA) on six screens (hospital-chart-preround, hospital-chart-encounter, hospital-add, nh-chart-preround, nh-chart-encounter, and /snf/add, which the visual lane never captured) on desktop Chromium 1280x800, Pixel 7 Chromium and iPhone 15 WebKit (18 captures, fresh @roundai.test account, no model). The three controls the scenario names are clean on every screen and profile: the status select is named 'Admission status' (4 chart screens x 3 profiles), the Note Format picker is named 'Note Format' (Hospital: H&P / SOAP progress / Consult note / Discharge summary; Nursing Home: SNF admission / SNF follow-up), both add forms' Encounter Type select is named by its label, and axe reports no violation on any of them. Other axe violations on these screens, identical on all three profiles: color-contrast (serious) on 5 of 6 screens (1-16 nodes: section headings, hints, a 10 px button on the Hospital Encounter tab; A4) and button-name (critical) on the Nursing Home chart's back arrow on both NH chart screens (A1, known). So 'no WCAG 2 A/AA violations on the listed screens' does not hold, but every violation is a known suggestion (A1/A4), none is on the named controls."},"testCase":{"id":"a613da36b11541b941f67c49bd481a49","externalId":"3eef56c5e95a671a00248fb72b943918","name":"[local] S21 axe on the badge control, the Note Format picker and both add forms","fullName":"TC-06 Admission Status Toggle › TC-06/S21"},"descriptionHtml":"<p><b>Case priority: P2 · extra (accessibility, performance, prototype detail)</b> · ours: accessibility (axe, named controls).</p><div class=\"rc-approach\"><p><b>Approach</b> · TC-06 Admission Status Toggle · <b>S21</b> axe on the badge control, the Note Format picker and both add forms</p><p><b>UAT steps / ticket ACs covered:</b></p><ul><li><b>U3</b> The manual add form has the three-state toggle (New Admission / Follow-up / Consult) at creation, it defaults to Follow-up, and the state chosen there (or left untouched) is the one saved (UAT TC-06; TFA-92584 AC 2; TFA-92584 AC 3)</li><li><b>U4</b> The physician can change the badge by hand at any time (before or after Generate, and on a patient whose status already rolled) through all three states, and each change persists (list, chart, reload … (UAT TC-06; TFA-92584 AC 1)</li><li><b>U8</b> The badge pre-selects the template at Generate: Hospital New Admission -&gt; H&amp;P, Follow-up -&gt; SOAP progress, Consult -&gt; Consult note; … (UAT TC-06; TFA-92584 AC 6; TFA-92584 AC 7)</li></ul><p><b>Test design technique: </b>Accessibility (accessibility) — Check screen-reader, keyboard, contrast and tap-size rules (axe): users with disabilities have to be able to use it too.</p><p><b>Given </b>Visual lane fixture, both contexts</p><p><b>When </b>Run axe on hospital-chart-preround, hospital-chart-encounter, hospital-add, nh-chart-preround, nh-chart-encounter and /snf/add</p><p><b>Then </b>No WCAG 2 A/AA violations on the listed screens, including named form controls (the status select, the add-form toggle and Note Format)</p><p><b>Pass rule (oracle, excerpt): </b>axe-core violations = 0 (visual-checks.ts) on the listed screens. From code reading on e02167f, not checked by this scenario: the status select is named 'Admission status' and the badge picture is aria-hidden (PatientCard.tsx AdmissionStatusControl); …</p><p><b>Where it ran: </b>local newspec-c (new Playwright specs); test method VISUAL · Visual (screenshots for a person); lane planned in the matrix: visual / mobile (automated)</p><p><small>S21 is our own case number (its number in the coverage matrix cases/TC-06.matrix.json), not a step number of the UAT document.</small></p></div><p><b>Environment: local</b> — main e02167f → 8b4be94a (10-20 re-run), local stack (not a deployed build); run folder <code>runs/2026-10-14-local</code>, lane newspec-c.</p><p><b>Test method:</b> VISUAL · Visual (screenshots for a person) — as classified in cases/test-methods.json, which says it runs on both; Source: <code>newspec-c</code>.</p><p><b>UAT item:</b> TC-06 Admission Status Toggle · <b>Section:</b> A1 · Home Screen &amp; Dashboard · <b>Scenario:</b> TC-06/S21</p><p><b>axe on the badge control, the Note Format picker and both add forms</b></p><p><b>Tickets:</b> TFA-92584 Admission Status Toggle (ready for qa)</p><p><b>New local lane</b> <code>newspec-c</code>: status <b>record-only</b> in <code>newspec-c/results.json</code> → <b>passed</b> (record only (every judged cell passed, the rest is recorded only)).</p><p><b>Detail:</b></p><pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">Our own addition (no UAT item or ticket asks for axe): record-only, findings are suggestions. Spec newspec-c/vis-tc06-s21-s22-badge-visual.spec.ts ran axe-core 4.14 (WCAG 2 A/AA) on six screens (hospital-chart-preround, hospital-chart-encounter, hospital-add, nh-chart-preround, nh-chart-encounter, and /snf/add, which the visual lane never captured) on desktop Chromium 1280x800, Pixel 7 Chromium and iPhone 15 WebKit (18 captures, fresh @roundai.test account, no model). The three controls the scenario names are clean on every screen and profile: the status select is named 'Admission status' (4 chart screens x 3 profiles), the Note Format picker is named 'Note Format' (Hospital: H&amp;P / SOAP progress / Consult note / Discharge summary; Nursing Home: SNF admission / SNF follow-up), both add forms' Encounter Type select is named by its label, and axe reports no violation on any of them. Other axe violations on these screens, identical on all three profiles: color-contrast (serious) on 5 of 6 screens (1-16 nodes: section headings, hints, a 10 px button on the Hospital Encounter tab; A4) and button-name (critical) on the Nursing Home chart's back arrow on both NH chart screens (A1, known). So 'no WCAG 2 A/AA violations on the listed screens' does not hold, but every violation is a known suggestion (A1/A4), none is on the named controls.</pre><p><b>Evidence:</b> 39 attached.</p><p><b>Dev run:</b> skipped: not runnable on dev — not-runnable-on-dev: visual-screens — Lane V (visual-lane.ts, local fixture).. This local result replaces that dev entry (the scenario appears once).</p>","environment":"default","setup":[],"teardown":[],"history":[],"retries":[],"breadcrumbs":[["TC-06 Admission Status Toggle","S21 axe on the badge control, the Note Format picker and both add forms"]],"retry":false,"titlePath":[],"retriesCount":0,"attachments":[{"link":{"used":true,"missed":false,"id":"19200dabe9d0d805b0736b56d1c5e374","originalFileName":"14164e12-ac75-4ad4-a19b-7309d50028d9-attachment.json","ext":".json","contentType":"application/json","contentLength":1690,"name":"newspec-c/evidence/tc06-s21-s22-desktop-hospital-add.json"},"type":"attachment"},{"link":{"used":true,"missed":false,"id":"507e